From 581cbee0ed7b086d84e94f9a20b4e513fe5be013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Release Radar <release-radar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:47:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Stream cache, two positions per book, playback
 diagnostics

Streamed audio now passes through a 768 MB on-disk cache keyed by file (not
by the per-session URL), so the index at the head of the file and the audio
around the playhead come from the phone on the next start. The load control
keeps ten minutes ahead while paused; a pre-buffer (off on metered networks,
cancellable, with a no-progress watchdog) writes the window around the other
position of the book, so the way back is instant too. Every track of a
multi-file book goes through the same factory (cache, home route, retry).

Two positions, the Audible way: the phone records where it left each book;
when a session starts at the synced position another device moved to, or
play is pressed after a longer pause and the server is ahead (checked first,
never waiting more than 2 s), playback continues from the synced position
and the player menu offers the way back to this phone's position.

Playback diagnostics go to the log page: audio focus and suppression, player
and device volume (edges only), audio outputs coming and going, sink and
decoder errors, underruns, a heartbeat every five minutes while playing.

Home-network route: the route is tied to the exact (canonical, home) pair
it was verified for and every probe re-proves the same server; a cancelled
request or a non-connect error no longer marks the home address down; a
held-off probe is deferred, not dropped; the account page saves only the
address (no stale token written back).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

